// The load-bearing half of "a tier block's `use` drives linking": because the block's imports now
// go through the same resolution a top-level `use` does, an import naming **no such module** is a
// link error — at check time, with the usual "did you mean" over the modules that do exist.
//
// Before the fix the block's `use` was never resolved at all, so this program checked **clean**
// (0 errors) and failed only at `noeta test`, at every use site, with "cannot find type
// `probe.nope.Missing` in this scope" — a runtime symptom for a plainly static mistake, pointing at
// the uses rather than at the typo. This case is the one shape of the bug the harness can observe
// without activating a tier, so it is what pins the fix: it fails on the pre-fix loader.
//
// The error is reported inside the block, where it is written, even though the block itself is
// stripped for a run with no tier active.
// expect: error E0019 at 18:21
// expect: exit 1
namespace App.Main;

@test {
    use probe.nope.{Missing}

    fn builds(): void {
        x = Missing { n: 3 }
        assert(x.n == 3)
    }
}

echo "unreachable — the link fails"
